Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:05.00,Film,,0,0,0,,EuroRollup shows how crypto trades and fund investments settle in euros.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.00,0:00:14.00,Film,,0,0,0,,Starting with a thousand demo euros, I buy two hundred euros of test ether. The receipt shows the five-cent charge.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.00,0:00:22.00,Film,,0,0,0,,My fund order waits for its valuation. At ninety-six euros per unit, three hundred euros buys three and one eighth units.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.00,0:00:33.00,Film,,0,0,0,,Now I ask what happens if Friday's fund cutoff moves from four to three. The model turns my question into one proposed rule.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.00,0:00:44.00,Film,,0,0,0,,I confirm the change and replay two orders. The earlier one still settles Friday. The three-thirty order now waits until Monday.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.00,0:00:55.00,Film,,0,0,0,,That leaves three hundred extra euros reserved over the weekend. On Monday the later order receives three units. Both outcomes come with a reproducible record.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.00,0:01:00.00,Film,,0,0,0,,Open the project on GitHub and replay the experiment yourself.
